<title>INDIA: India Colour-Chem 96/97 1st half net up.</title>
<headline>India Colour-Chem 96/97 1st half net up.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	  137.5  vs    110.2</p>
<p>    Net sales	 1,414.2  vs  1,362.5</p>
<p>    Other income	 61.7  vs     55.2</p>
<p>    Expenditure     1,182.4  vs  1,187.0</p>
<p>    Interest costs     64.3  vs     50.6</p>
<p>    Gross profit	229.2  vs    180.1</p>
<p>    Depreciation	 41.7  vs     32.4</p>
<p>    Tax		    50.0  vs     37.5</p>
<p>    *Share (in rupees)236.0  vs    163.0</p>
<p>Note:Colour-Chem Ltd, the Indian subsidiary of Hoechst AG, said the results are unaudited.</p>
<p>* The earning per share figure is annualised.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91-22-265 9000)</p>
</text>
